        "original_id": "38d3fd20-a83f-5c10-b2e3-0de0db3ad11c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Independent Commission on the Voting System, Jenkins Commission\n- People: Roy Jenkins\n- Systems: Alternative Vote Plus, mixed electoral systems, mixed-member proportional representation, Additional Member System, majority bonus system\n- Places: United Kingdom\n- Topics: electoral reform, United Kingdom electoral system\n\nFacts:\n- Roy Jenkins, formally Roy Harris Jenkins, Baron Jenkins of Hillhead, was born on 11 November 1920 and died on 5 January 2003.\n- Roy Jenkins was a British Labour Party, SDP, and Liberal Democrat politician and a biographer of British political leaders.\n- The Independent Commission on the Voting System was popularly known as the Jenkins Commission after its chairman Roy Jenkins.\n- The Independent Commission on the Voting System examined possible reform of the United Kingdom electoral system.\n- In 1998, the Jenkins Commission devised Alternative Vote Plus and first proposed it as a system for elections to the Parliament of the United Kingdom.\n- Alternative Vote Plus is one of the most common mixed electoral systems, alongside mixed-member proportional representation, the Additional Member System, and the majority bonus system.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
